!.pHive/specialist-phases/performance:audit/kg-signal-revival/
!.pHive/specialist-phases/performance:audit/kg-signal-revival/**
# Metrics carrier (.pHive/metrics/) — authored by S2 stories of the
# meta-improvement-system epic; contains schema docs and, from C1.4 on,
# fixtures consumed by hive/lib/metrics/ unit tests.
!.pHive/metrics/
!.pHive/metrics/**
# Per-session stop-hook event files are runtime artifacts (one per session)
# that accumulate locally and should never be tracked — they leak session IDs
# and explode the diff on every PR. Meta-* / agent-spawn-* fixtures stay tracked.
.pHive/metrics/events/stop-*.jsonl
.pHive/metrics/events/agent-spawn-runtime-*.jsonl
# MVL proof artifacts — only the canonical mvl-proof folder ships with the repo.
!.pHive/audits/
.pHive/audits/*
!.pHive/audits/mvl-proof/
!.pHive/audits/mvl-proof/**
!.pHive/audits/mvs-proof/
!.pHive/audits/mvs-proof/**
# Post-run audits for /plan + /execute (gate-mode telemetry). Tracked so
# cross-run aggregation (hive/scripts/gate-mode-audit.mjs) sees a stable corpus.
!.pHive/audits/post-run/
!.pHive/audits/post-run/**
!.pHive/audits/smoke-test/
!.pHive/audits/smoke-test/**
!.pHive/audits/plugin-install-payload/
!.pHive/audits/plugin-install-payload/**
# Consumer-side executor flag (hde-9a Q4 lock). Tracked because the maintainer
# repo doubles as the canonical consumer for plugin-hive itself; consumers of
# the plugin choose whether to commit their own .pHive/hive.config.yaml.
!.pHive/hive.config.yaml
# Consumer-side per-workflow graduation registry (hde-9b). Same maintainer-
# as-canonical-consumer rationale as the flag above; other content under
# .pHive/runtime/ stays ignored.
!.pHive/runtime/
.pHive/runtime/*
!.pHive/runtime/executor-graduated-workflows.yaml
agents/memories/
.claude/settings.local.json
.history/
.DS_Store
*.log
.claude/*.lock
.sandcastle/
# Python bytecode/caches — C1.4 (hive/lib/metrics/) introduced Python 3 runtime
# primitives with stdlib-only deps. Prevent __pycache__/ and *.pyc files from
# polluting the tree as future maintainer tooling adds more Python.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Single-file domain glossary (story a-26-context-md-schema-and-starter).
# This file IS tracked — it serves as plugin-hive own CONTEXT.md and as
# an exemplar for downstream projects.
!.pHive/CONTEXT.md
# upstream-watch: durable upstream blocker records tracked at maintainer level.
!.pHive/upstream-watch/
!.pHive/upstream-watch/**
# Logo exploration artifacts (story ulo-4-artifact-conventions).
# Brand artifacts are local-by-default: the maintainer decides what to track
# by adding explicit `!.pHive/brand/<path>` allow-rules below. The
# logo-explorations dir IS tracked (prompts.md / contact-sheet.html /
# selected.yaml stay reviewable in git); only the generated PNG candidates
# are ignored (large binaries, regeneratable from prompts.md).
!.pHive/brand/
.pHive/brand/*
!.pHive/brand/logo-explorations/
!.pHive/brand/logo-explorations/**
.pHive/brand/logo-explorations/**/*.png
# To track additional brand assets (e.g., finalized logo package), add an
# explicit allow-rule here, like: `!.pHive/brand/logo/` and `!.pHive/brand/logo/**`.

# Local dev — better-sqlite3 transient install for kg bootstrap (BYO enhancement)
node_modules/

# Task-tracking-dispatch test fixture artifacts (generated by tests, not source)
hive/lib/task-tracking-dispatch/.pHive-test/

